      en: "The Al-Hazm Plateau is a rocky plateau in central Bahrain, known for its desert vegetation and geological formations. Covering about 10 km², it reaches an elevation of 80 meters above sea level. It provides habitat for desert animals like gazelles and foxes. The area is also known for fossil discoveries. The plateau is a popular destination for hikers and geologists.",
